@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* The landing page's frame: the page itself and nothing around it.

   The landing page is public marketing, and the design draws it with a header and a footer of its
   own rather than inside the application's sidebar - so it does not sit in MainLayout's shell. The
   page brings its own header, language switch and way in. AuthLayout nests here for the same
   reason: the sign-in and register screens are public pages too, and share this boundary and this
   dock.

   The page's failures pass through the one boundary, as every screen in MainLayout's do.

   The connection dock stays, for the reason MainLayout keeps it outside its grid: it belongs to the
   circuit rather than to any screen, and the landing page runs on a circuit like every other. The
   sign-in and register screens have no circuit for it to report on, so on them it stays at its
   hidden default: they carry it only because this layout does, as NotFound, AccessDenied and Error
   carry MainLayout's. *@

<SessionExpiryBoundary>
    @Body
</SessionExpiryBoundary>

<DtConnectionDock />
